{"diagnosis": "Loopback read via picosoc/picosoc.v:124 / picosoc/picosoc.v:204 got 0xff vs expected 0xa5, i.e. `reg_dat_do` returned `~0` per line 53 so `recv_buf_valid==0`. Root cause in excerpt line 68: reset sets `recv_state <= 1` instead of idle 0 (lines 77-82 `if (!ser_rx)`), so `recv_divcnt` counts to `2*recv_divcnt > cfg_divider` (lines 83-86) without a start bit and the true frame is missed, never setting `recv_buf_valid`.",
"patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@
 	always @(posedge clk) begin
 		if (!resetn) begin
-			recv_state <= 1;
+			recv_state <= 0;
 			recv_divcnt <= 0;
 			recv_pattern <= 0;
 			recv_buf_data <= 0;",
"expected": "tohost PASS (no FAIL 0xdead, no TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xff want 0xa5, loopback 0xa5 matches)"}

